cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Theoryscope in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Theoryscope: renormalisation group theory and eigenvector analysis for intellectual history"
abstract: >-
  Renormalisation group theory and eigenvector analysis brought to intellectual history
  and critical theory as a critical method, applied to a corpus of theoretical texts.
  Part of the Vector Lab family of research instruments.
  Built at Copenhagen Business School, Denmark, during an Otto Mønsted Visiting Professorship
  in 2026. The support of the Otto Mønsted Fond (grant 25-12-1849) is gratefully acknowledged.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Berry
    given-names: David M.
    affiliation: University of Sussex
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7737-5586"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vector-lab-tools/theoryscope"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: "0.8.4"
date-released: 2026-11-12
keywords:
  - critical theory
  - intellectual history
  - renormalisation group
  - embeddings
  - digital humanities
